From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:46:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: preserve desktop platform registers

Keep the existing shared desktop machine's ECAM, GPIO power button,
ACPI reset page and watchdog interrupt. These registers are part of
its firmware contract alongside the PCI and GPU transports. Linux
profiles retain their existing platform layout.

Port the required power devices from Droid-VM 34fb0df12 and
2235c9334, without the latter's optional SBSA UART or serial backends.
The existing memory preparation argument identifies these profiles;
no additional machine-selection option is introduced.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 release build; GPIO power and ACPI reset event tests

Purpose: Preserve desktop platform registers.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
